Register each sign-in identity when the workbench creates it.

The native callback relay accepts only identities registered by the workbench,
so an unrelated outgoing address cannot replace or reserve a callback nonce.
Requests created before bridge initialization wait in a bounded private queue.
The bridge-ready event flushes that queue and reports registration failure
explicitly before deferred browser launches are released.

The provider also owns an immutable document identity so a queued return cannot
be delivered into a replacement page that reuses the same numeric request id.

